<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teutonic Order</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1190">1190</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Teutonic Knights, Order of the Teutonic Knights</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Teutonic Order is a Catholic military order founded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> around 1190 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>. From the 1230s it conquered the pagan Prussians and built a state on the Baltic, absorbing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> in 1237 and taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a> in 1308. Its defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> at Grunwald in 1410 began its decline, and in 1525 its Prussian lands became the secular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teutonic-order.jpg" alt="Teutonic Order" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Insignia_Germany_Order_Teutonic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
